# Secrets — never commit
.bunny.env
.evomi.env

# Generated / scraped data — never commit (huge, and RockAuto-owned images)
assets/parts/
artifacts/
ingest_ec2/out/
out/
coverage/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local run state
.auto_sync_state.json
.brand_load_state.json
.bunny_upload_state.json
*_state.json

# Ingest work queues + shards (transient, multi-GB). ingest_ec2/out/ above was too narrow —
# the solo/shard dirs held 6.1 GB of NDJSON and would otherwise be committable.
ingest_ec2/solo/
ingest_ec2/sh*/
ingest_ec2/p[0-9]*/
ingest_ec2/bunny_out/
ingest_ec2/*state*/
# Seeded frontiers + skip-sets are regenerable from the DB (bin/plan_targets.py), ~192 MB.
#
# EXCEPT plan/fr/ — it MUST ship. It is only 6.3 MB and it is the ONLY thing that tells
# the GitHub Actions fleet which work is left. While it was ignored, Actions could not see
# it, silently fell back to a whole-catalog sweep, and spent 105,000 requests to gain
# 13,342 new fitments (1.09 rows/request against the 4.445 these frontiers deliver).
# "Regenerable from the DB" is true on this laptop and false on a runner.
!plan/fr/
plan/fr_old/
plan/skip/
visited*.txt
gw_endpoints*.txt
.awstmp/
.gcp/
